WEBVTT

01:02.250 --> 01:04.333
It started as a tropical disturbance,

01:04.416 --> 01:07.541
but in the last 24 hours,
Henry became a Category 2 hurricane…

01:07.625 --> 01:10.666
From the 11:00 a.m.
advisory from the National…

01:10.750 --> 01:13.750
…has Annieville
in the crosshairs of Henry.

01:13.833 --> 01:15.750
This is expected to be a major…

01:15.833 --> 01:20.041
…a buzz saw on satellite,
as it beelines toward our coast.

01:20.125 --> 01:23.208
It shows the storm
making landfall near Annieville.

01:23.291 --> 01:26.000
This is nothing to mess around with.

01:26.083 --> 01:29.083
This is the harbormaster
out of Beaufort Weather Tower.

01:29.166 --> 01:30.625
The National Hurricane Center

01:30.708 --> 01:33.458
issued hurricane
and storm-surge warnings for this area.

01:33.541 --> 01:38.041
I repeat, hurricane and storm warnings
have been issued for this area.

01:38.125 --> 01:41.166
Winds of up to 150 knots, seas to 60 feet,

01:41.250 --> 01:44.083
and a 15-to-20-foot storm surge
are to be expected.

01:44.166 --> 01:47.500
Weather threats
ramping up throughout the day--

01:48.625 --> 01:50.333
Save our planet!

01:50.416 --> 01:53.708
It's the only one
with George, Garth, and Luke and Kate.

01:53.791 --> 01:57.291
-Come on, now! Save us.
-97.8, WVD…

02:36.916 --> 02:38.541
Hey, Ray, how's it going?

02:40.541 --> 02:45.000
Yeah, yeah, good. So, uh, today,
I was thinking something healthy.

02:45.083 --> 02:46.250
Like a burger.

02:47.750 --> 02:49.958
I mean, it still comes with tomato, right?

02:50.791 --> 02:53.666
Mm-hmm. Yeah, no rush.
Just send it over as soon as…

02:55.500 --> 02:56.625
Closing?

02:57.416 --> 02:58.458
Now?

03:00.541 --> 03:01.916
But…

03:02.000 --> 03:04.291
I mean, it's just a little bit of…

03:05.916 --> 03:06.875
rain.

03:10.416 --> 03:14.708
The grocery stores are still open, huh?
I guess I could just…

03:21.083 --> 03:23.041
Yeah, I guess I could just walk.

03:25.291 --> 03:27.333
Yeah, all right, stay safe.

03:27.416 --> 03:29.125
Mm-hmm. You too, bye.

03:38.875 --> 03:39.958
Get in.

03:40.916 --> 03:41.750
Good.

03:41.833 --> 03:43.708
-Gotta go.
-All right.

03:43.791 --> 03:47.000
I've got half a tank!

03:53.958 --> 03:55.875
Whoa! Dakota!

03:57.458 --> 04:00.208
You shouldn't be out here. It's not safe.

04:00.291 --> 04:01.291
I needed food.

04:01.375 --> 04:03.708
I haven't seen you in forever.

04:03.791 --> 04:05.541
Not since your mom passed.

04:06.541 --> 04:09.083
Look, they're saying
we should all get out of town.

04:11.791 --> 04:14.166
We got room in the car.

04:18.083 --> 04:19.208
Huh…

04:19.291 --> 04:21.583
Mm…

04:28.708 --> 04:31.125
Woo-hoo!

04:35.833 --> 04:41.125
That looks like an 8.5
for my man, Ron Olsen!

04:41.208 --> 04:43.541
Ron!

04:43.625 --> 04:46.833
Well burning the rubber
On my back tires…

04:47.666 --> 04:50.250
-Ron!
-Ron!

04:51.833 --> 04:53.875
Ron?

04:54.708 --> 04:56.708
Hey, stop fooling around, Ron.

04:57.833 --> 04:58.750
Ron!

04:58.833 --> 05:01.791
I gotta keep moving on down the road

05:01.875 --> 05:04.625
Gotcha!

05:04.708 --> 05:07.125
The highwayman…

05:07.208 --> 05:08.916
It's the aqua-lungs, baby.

05:11.791 --> 05:13.291
This rain won't let up.

05:14.125 --> 05:15.833
Three more days of this.

05:16.666 --> 05:19.333
-Then school.
-I don't wanna think about it.

05:19.416 --> 05:21.708
Well, at least we gonna get fed every day.

05:24.041 --> 05:25.708
Okay, Will, you're up.

05:25.791 --> 05:28.500
Hold on. Quick gator-and-snake check.

05:28.583 --> 05:30.083
-Safety first.
-All right.

05:32.250 --> 05:34.916
We're good. Bombs away.

05:39.125 --> 05:43.000
What the hell do y'all think you're doing?
Get on down, little bastards!

05:45.333 --> 05:47.625
Don't you know
there's snakes in these swamps?

05:49.958 --> 05:51.625
Dee was on lookout, Mr. Olson.

05:52.625 --> 05:56.500
On lookout. What's she gonna be doing?
Spotting cottonmouths from up there?

05:56.583 --> 06:00.166
Who do you think's picking up
the goddamn doctor's bill?

06:00.250 --> 06:01.375
I'll tell you who.

06:01.458 --> 06:04.833
-Billy Olson right here.
-Like you'd ever take us to the doctor.

06:04.916 --> 06:06.500
What'd you say?

06:07.291 --> 06:09.375
What'd you say?

06:10.375 --> 06:13.416
Nothing, that's right.
Get your asses in the truck right now.

06:37.333 --> 06:38.500
All right.

06:40.000 --> 06:40.958
Come on.

07:01.625 --> 07:03.458
-Hey.
-Lisa, you're still here.

07:03.541 --> 07:06.666
But not for long.
I thought everything was closing down?

07:06.750 --> 07:11.125
Yeah, boss man wanted me to do
another load before they call it a day.

07:11.208 --> 07:13.625
Guess who's getting overtime?

07:13.708 --> 07:15.375
Where's Eric? He in the back?

07:15.458 --> 07:18.291
All right, Bob, see you later. Drive safe.

07:18.375 --> 07:19.458
Yeah, you too.

07:23.625 --> 07:25.500
The wind is so strong.

07:25.583 --> 07:30.083
Now those waves will come out to be
maybe six or even seven feet tall.

07:33.000 --> 07:34.875
No, I haven't told anyone yet.

07:34.958 --> 07:36.458
Lisa, honey.

07:36.541 --> 07:38.041
Mom, it's embarrassing.

07:38.125 --> 07:40.375
How is it embarrassing for you?

07:40.458 --> 07:42.458
The jerk who left his pregnant fiancée

07:42.541 --> 07:45.208
to become, what,
a professional poker player?

07:45.291 --> 07:47.083
Yep. And a DJ.

07:47.166 --> 07:50.083
After he asked you to move
a thousand miles to his town?

07:50.166 --> 07:51.541
Ya know, I knew it.

07:51.625 --> 07:55.791
I knew it the moment I laid eyes
on that no-good son of a bitch.

07:55.875 --> 08:00.250
-Can we just not talk about him?
-Honey, did you give it any more thought?

08:00.333 --> 08:01.875
-What?
-You know, the birth.

08:01.958 --> 08:05.583
Like doing it in the tub,
in the water, like your sister did?

08:05.666 --> 08:07.666
-Mom.
-It'll still be in a hospital.

08:07.750 --> 08:11.625
Yes, yes, in room 202 in a big, comfy bed

08:11.708 --> 08:14.833
with my perfectly-curated birth playlist.

08:14.916 --> 08:18.166
Wait, why haven't you left town yet?

08:18.250 --> 08:20.666
They said the storm's gonna be really big.

08:20.750 --> 08:24.750
They made us come into work today.
It wasn't my choice, but I'm leaving now.

08:24.833 --> 08:28.291
How you gonna do that?
They said they closed the interstate.

08:29.375 --> 08:30.291
Wait, what?

08:30.375 --> 08:32.166
They just closed the interstate.

08:32.250 --> 08:34.666
Honey, you gotta get to higher ground.

08:39.916 --> 08:40.958
Go, go, go!

08:41.958 --> 08:44.833
Dale, how bad is it out there?

08:44.916 --> 08:45.916
Pretty bad.

08:46.000 --> 08:50.458
Every fish south of Bermuda is bolting
north to get away from this storm.

08:50.541 --> 08:52.000
Must be a big one.

08:53.208 --> 08:55.541
Oh, yeah, that's coming in fast too.

08:57.791 --> 09:00.916
-Hey, did you get everyone tagged?
-Not even close.

09:01.000 --> 09:04.250
Too many of them
seem to be coming in with the storm.

09:04.333 --> 09:07.166
-Too many of them?
-The bull sharks.

09:07.250 --> 09:10.166
Spotted at least six
before I had to get out of there.

09:10.250 --> 09:12.625
Must be seeking shelter
in freshwater estuaries.

09:12.708 --> 09:14.416
-Dr. Edwards?
-Greg.

09:14.500 --> 09:16.375
-Hey.
-Thanks for the heads-up.

09:16.458 --> 09:18.166
-Of course.
-How bad is it?

09:23.500 --> 09:27.916
Yeah. If they ever consider
creating a Category 6, this would be it.

09:28.000 --> 09:29.458
It is a monster.

09:29.541 --> 09:31.833
-What are they calling it?
-Hurricane Henry.

09:32.958 --> 09:33.791
Henry.

09:34.708 --> 09:35.916
What would you call it?

09:36.541 --> 09:38.833
Uh… Ted Bundy?

09:39.750 --> 09:40.666
Oh.

09:40.750 --> 09:42.875
I've got to get hold of my niece.

09:43.916 --> 09:45.166
Okay, good idea.

09:59.750 --> 10:01.500
-Hey.
-You okay?

10:01.583 --> 10:03.416
Yeah, I was just, um…

10:05.208 --> 10:06.166
What's up?

10:06.250 --> 10:09.666
I was just calling to make sure
you have some way of leaving town.

10:09.750 --> 10:11.958
If not, I could come pick you up in a bit.

10:12.708 --> 10:16.833
-Thanks, but no need. I'm staying.
-They're saying it could be a Category 5.

10:16.916 --> 10:20.083
It could land right on top of Annieville.
Which means

10:20.166 --> 10:21.916
the house might come down on you.

10:22.000 --> 10:24.166
You could be swimming inside your bedroom.

10:24.250 --> 10:26.000
I dunno. Sounds kinda fun.

10:27.041 --> 10:28.708
Look, you said it yourself.

10:29.291 --> 10:31.291
"Could" or "might."

10:32.541 --> 10:35.625
It's what they always say,
and everything turns out fine.

10:35.708 --> 10:37.333
The house is safe.

10:38.541 --> 10:39.791
And so am I.

10:39.875 --> 10:42.291
Look, I know you're hurting, Dakota.

10:42.375 --> 10:44.125
I miss your mother every day.

10:44.208 --> 10:47.708
But hiding in that house isn't going
to make the hurt go away.

10:55.291 --> 10:58.958
You really suck at this parenting stuff.

10:59.666 --> 11:02.166
What can I say? I'm new at it.

11:03.125 --> 11:06.041
Yeah, I know.

11:06.125 --> 11:08.250
I'll be there as soon as I can, okay?

11:08.333 --> 11:10.458
It'll only take a couple of hours.

11:11.708 --> 11:12.583
Deal?

11:13.333 --> 11:14.500
Deal.

11:34.250 --> 11:36.333
You kids even listening to me?

11:36.416 --> 11:38.666
I'm telling you, in fact, I swear to God,

11:38.750 --> 11:42.083
you pull any of that shit again,
I'll send you back to foster care.

11:42.166 --> 11:43.666
Stay tuned for…

11:43.750 --> 11:47.166
Little shits, you don't know
your asses from a hole in the ground.

11:47.250 --> 11:50.916
Law enforcement
have issued a mandatory evacuation,

11:51.000 --> 11:53.375
telling residents
they must leave their homes

11:53.458 --> 11:56.916
as the storm surge is expected
to hit shores within the next hour.

11:57.000 --> 11:58.791
Lots of folks taking off.

11:58.875 --> 12:01.333
-Breaking at this hour…
-Are we heading out too?

12:01.416 --> 12:05.458
Bullshit, we are.
Ain't nothing but a little bit of weather.

12:05.541 --> 12:09.583
Wind and rain, and these jokers dump a log
in their panties, run for the hills.

12:09.666 --> 12:10.875
…biggest threat with…

12:12.208 --> 12:15.416
If it don't twang, it ain't my thing

12:15.500 --> 12:19.708
If it don't hang
Like the midnight train

12:19.791 --> 12:22.041
Or cry like a steel

12:22.125 --> 12:24.875
Bending my old heartstrings

12:24.958 --> 12:28.000
Listen! I said Brooke is your mother's--

12:28.083 --> 12:31.041
Get your finger out of my face!

12:31.125 --> 12:32.708
-Out!
-All!

12:32.791 --> 12:36.375
-I'm not crazy! You were eating my face!
-Gotta get out of the room.

12:36.458 --> 12:39.500
-No, absolutely not.
-Call the police right now.

12:40.333 --> 12:43.791
Look at the radar
of Hurricane Henry one hour ago.

12:43.875 --> 12:47.583
It's a Category 2, and then it hits
record warm waters off the coast,

12:47.666 --> 12:51.041
and boom, it becomes a Category 5.

12:51.916 --> 12:55.250
Two swimmers were attacked
on Myrtle Beach this morning

12:55.333 --> 12:58.000
by what onlookers say was a large shark.

13:01.083 --> 13:04.250
-Get her!
-Gonna get you!

13:07.958 --> 13:12.750
-That's my girl.
-Okay, let me show you.

13:12.833 --> 13:13.833
Okay.

13:15.666 --> 13:18.041
See? It's stable.

13:18.125 --> 13:20.458
Much easier to hit.

13:20.541 --> 13:22.583
One more time?

13:22.666 --> 13:24.625
-You try.
-Okay.

13:24.708 --> 13:26.750
You can do it. Good.

13:26.833 --> 13:29.333
Try your dad.

13:30.291 --> 13:32.083
Oh, boy. Ow!

13:32.166 --> 13:34.250
-Bull's-eye!
-Yes!

13:34.333 --> 13:37.458
You got him.

13:37.541 --> 13:38.958
You're amazing.

14:01.583 --> 14:03.416
What if the windows break?

14:03.500 --> 14:05.416
Reinforced glass, all right?

14:05.500 --> 14:08.416
I installed them bad boys myself.

14:08.500 --> 14:11.666
That, the waterproof wiring,
and a generator.

14:12.333 --> 14:14.375
So quit your goddamn worrying.

14:19.375 --> 14:20.750
It's coming down out there!

14:20.833 --> 14:24.833
I caught them little bastards
up by the creek swimming with damn snakes.

14:24.916 --> 14:28.208
Swear to God, they do not have
the sense they were born with.

14:28.291 --> 14:29.875
Do not know why I bother.

14:29.958 --> 14:32.791
Oh, need I remind you, baby, huh? Huh?

14:32.875 --> 14:35.291
Uncle Sam, he does pay out now and then.

14:35.375 --> 14:36.375
Yeah.

14:36.458 --> 14:37.458
We're hungry.

14:37.541 --> 14:39.833
-Goddamn!
-Where did you come from?

14:41.291 --> 14:43.125
Are those steaks?

14:44.750 --> 14:46.541
It's none of your damn business!

14:48.875 --> 14:49.916
Here.

14:51.416 --> 14:53.708
Just like Mama used to make.

14:54.291 --> 14:57.833
Hey, you know goddamn well
that this basement's off-limits.

14:58.416 --> 15:00.166
-Right.
-Get your ass up there.

15:08.166 --> 15:11.750
Dr. Edwards! Do you mind
if we speak to you for a moment?

15:13.166 --> 15:16.958
Sorry, just… Any comment
on the shark incident this morning?

15:17.541 --> 15:18.375
What incident?

15:19.375 --> 15:22.958
A couple at Myrtle Beach
was attacked by a great white shark.

15:23.041 --> 15:26.791
Eyewitnesses saw the whole thing,
spotted at least two sharks on the scene.

15:26.875 --> 15:28.750
Great whites don't hunt in packs.

15:28.833 --> 15:31.208
What you're describing
sounds like bull sharks.

15:31.291 --> 15:35.375
Bull sharks, yes. The hyenas of the ocean.

15:35.458 --> 15:37.750
Thrives in salt and fresh water,

15:37.833 --> 15:40.458
got 12 times as powerful bite
as most sharks,

15:40.541 --> 15:43.208
and eats about anything they come across.

15:43.291 --> 15:46.041
Not necessarily accurate
and greatly exaggerated.

15:46.125 --> 15:47.458
Thank you very much.

15:47.541 --> 15:48.666
-So…
-Come on.

15:48.750 --> 15:52.625
The risk of shark attacks is on the rise,
according to the expert.

16:01.416 --> 16:02.625
Hello?

16:04.041 --> 16:05.750
Anybody here?

16:06.625 --> 16:07.791
Hello?

16:07.875 --> 16:09.833
Fuck! Shit.

16:10.916 --> 16:13.708
Okay.

16:15.250 --> 16:16.750
-Hey.
-Honey?

16:16.833 --> 16:19.208
Honey, ha-- have you got a plan?

16:19.291 --> 16:21.208
Are you getting out of town?

16:21.291 --> 16:22.750
Mom, it's getting scary.

16:22.833 --> 16:24.250
I'm really worri--

16:26.166 --> 16:27.000
Mom?

16:35.041 --> 16:36.333
Breathe.

16:38.291 --> 16:39.875
Just breathe.

16:45.541 --> 16:46.791
Shit.

17:03.333 --> 17:07.125
Roads are already impassable.
If you choose to shelter in place,

17:07.208 --> 17:09.666
law enforcement
is telling residents that stayed

17:09.750 --> 17:13.125
to write their contact information
on their arm in permanent marker,

17:13.208 --> 17:16.666
so they'll be able to ID your body
once the storm passe--

17:59.000 --> 18:01.333
Shit!

18:03.541 --> 18:04.500
Lisa!

18:05.083 --> 18:06.083
Stop!

18:07.166 --> 18:09.041
-What?
-Turn around!

18:09.125 --> 18:10.166
What?

18:10.250 --> 18:13.583
That tree just came down,
nearly knocked me off the road!

18:13.666 --> 18:15.000
You gotta turn around!

18:17.041 --> 18:20.375
-You back up and follow me, okay?
-Okay.

18:42.708 --> 18:47.208
Lisa! Lisa, go! Go!
Try to squeeze through!

18:47.291 --> 18:48.583
Get to high ground!

18:59.958 --> 19:01.500
Come on!

19:06.208 --> 19:09.166
I can make it. Yeah, I can make it.

19:21.375 --> 19:22.375
Ah!

19:23.875 --> 19:25.000
Come on!

19:27.375 --> 19:28.791
Piece of shit!

19:28.875 --> 19:30.250
Come on!

19:32.666 --> 19:34.958
Oh, God! No!

19:42.250 --> 19:43.791
Fucking go!

19:43.875 --> 19:44.875
Fuck!

20:11.583 --> 20:13.458
Holy fucking shit.

20:27.083 --> 20:30.958
We are seeing the worst
of Henry's wind and surge right now.

20:31.041 --> 20:33.958
The tide gauge
at Annieville showed a 15-foot surge--

20:34.041 --> 20:35.041
What was that?

20:35.125 --> 20:38.333
I hope that everyone took
the evacuation order seriously.

20:44.500 --> 20:45.666
Whoa.

20:48.416 --> 20:49.458
Storm's here.

20:50.250 --> 20:52.833
-Mr. Olson?
-What?

20:53.416 --> 20:54.583
Billy?

20:54.666 --> 20:55.583
Mr. Olson!

20:55.666 --> 20:58.875
For fuck's sake,
I am not gonna say this again, okay?

20:58.958 --> 21:01.458
It's just a little bit of weather.

21:03.250 --> 21:04.458
Ow!

21:07.958 --> 21:08.791
Shit!

21:19.166 --> 21:21.125
Oh, fuck, fuck, fuck!

21:31.708 --> 21:32.666
Shit.

21:32.750 --> 21:33.750
Oh, no.

21:38.166 --> 21:39.958
Help! Help!

21:51.791 --> 21:53.083
Please!

21:54.208 --> 21:55.916
Please help!

22:28.416 --> 22:31.041
Water's gonna keep rising.
We cannot stay, Billy.

22:31.125 --> 22:34.500
So how we gonna get anywhere?
What are we gonna do? Fucking swim?

22:34.583 --> 22:36.875
-I don't know!
-What about the snorkel?

22:36.958 --> 22:39.333
Ain't that what the snorkel's for?

22:39.416 --> 22:41.833
Quit being a smart-ass, Ron. Snorkel!

22:41.916 --> 22:43.875
Sn-- No, the snorkel. On the car.

22:43.958 --> 22:47.083
No, no, no, hang on.
The boy's right. The car's got a snorkel.

22:47.166 --> 22:50.375
Yeah, man, that's the waterproof
power distribution pack I got.

22:51.583 --> 22:52.875
Yeah, man.

22:52.958 --> 22:55.166
That can handle it. Come on.

22:55.250 --> 22:57.083
Y'all wait here while we check.

23:01.291 --> 23:02.458
Oh my God!

23:03.500 --> 23:05.625
Holy shit!

23:05.708 --> 23:07.958
Can't see a damn thing!

23:08.041 --> 23:10.333
Ah!

23:11.791 --> 23:13.416
-Help!
-Whoa.

23:13.500 --> 23:15.958
-Help me!
-Hey, do you hear that?

23:16.041 --> 23:17.000
Hear what?

23:17.875 --> 23:18.958
I can't hear a thing.

23:19.041 --> 23:21.041
Help! Help me!

23:21.125 --> 23:23.166
There's someone out there!

23:24.458 --> 23:25.333
Help!

23:25.416 --> 23:26.875
-Over there!
-Where you going?

23:26.958 --> 23:28.791
-This way!
-Help!

23:28.875 --> 23:29.958
-Hey!
-Wait there!

23:30.041 --> 23:30.916
Help!

23:33.166 --> 23:34.500
Somebody!

23:35.958 --> 23:39.125
-Hey!
-Help! Help me!

23:39.208 --> 23:41.708
-Hey!
-Please help me!

23:41.791 --> 23:43.416
I'm coming!

23:43.500 --> 23:44.416
Help!

23:44.500 --> 23:46.250
Help! Help me!

23:46.333 --> 23:48.791
I got you. I got you. You all right?

23:48.875 --> 23:49.833
No, I'm stuck.

23:49.916 --> 23:51.083
Hang on!

23:54.041 --> 23:55.083
Come on.

23:56.708 --> 23:58.208
Whoa, oh!

24:00.833 --> 24:01.666
Come on.

24:01.750 --> 24:04.208
-Okay, okay.
-Please don't leave me.

24:04.291 --> 24:06.791
We'll find something
to cut you loose with.

24:06.875 --> 24:08.125
-Don't leave!
-Hey.

24:08.208 --> 24:10.833
Don't worry. I'm not going anywhere, okay?

24:12.666 --> 24:13.833
Hey, Jimmy!

24:13.916 --> 24:16.458
Go get them cutters!

24:16.541 --> 24:18.875
The big ones from the back of the truck!

24:23.625 --> 24:25.791
Hey, what's your name?

24:27.166 --> 24:28.875
Lisa… Lisa.

24:28.958 --> 24:32.250
Lisa? Hey, I'm Scott.

24:32.333 --> 24:33.333
Nice to meet you.

24:33.416 --> 24:35.208
Yeah. Okay.

24:35.291 --> 24:36.250
Jimmy!

24:37.291 --> 24:38.250
Come on!

24:38.333 --> 24:40.041
I got 'em!

24:40.125 --> 24:41.625
I'm coming back!

24:42.666 --> 24:46.208
Hey, we're gonna get you outta here.
I promise.

24:56.000 --> 24:57.208
Jimmy?

25:01.000 --> 25:02.041
Hey!

25:02.125 --> 25:03.875
Jimmy!

25:06.958 --> 25:09.541
-I'm coming back! It's all right.
-Wait.

25:09.625 --> 25:12.500
Wait. Wait! Wait!

25:12.583 --> 25:15.000
Come back! Come back!

25:15.583 --> 25:18.333
Come back! Hey!

25:19.458 --> 25:20.291
Jimmy.

25:26.208 --> 25:27.833
Hey, Jimmy!

25:31.208 --> 25:32.125
Jimmy!

25:33.750 --> 25:35.291
Oh, God!

25:36.500 --> 25:39.791
-Jimmy!
-He got my fucking arm!

25:44.041 --> 25:46.250
-Oh, God!
-Jimmy!

25:46.333 --> 25:48.166
Oh, God!

25:48.250 --> 25:49.625
Jimmy!

25:49.708 --> 25:51.750
Sha-- Shark!

25:53.375 --> 25:56.375
Shark! Shark! Shark!

25:57.083 --> 25:58.666
Swim!

25:58.750 --> 26:00.416
Swim!

26:19.958 --> 26:24.291
Shark! Shark! Shark!

26:24.375 --> 26:27.000
-Shark! Shark!
-Whoa!

26:27.083 --> 26:28.041
Swim!

26:31.750 --> 26:32.833
Shark!

26:41.500 --> 26:43.500
I got you!

26:50.000 --> 26:51.958
The coastguard issued a ban

26:52.041 --> 26:54.750
for watercrafts leaving port
for the next 12 hours

26:54.833 --> 26:57.541
due to intense winds
and dangerous currents.

26:57.625 --> 27:01.291
In addition, there are also reports
that the I-17 is flooded,

27:01.375 --> 27:04.541
and several cities and towns
are experiencing mass casualties

27:04.625 --> 27:05.958
from the rising water.

27:06.041 --> 27:08.166
I-17, not good.

27:08.250 --> 27:10.791
-Up toward Annieville, right?
-Yeah.

27:14.375 --> 27:16.708
Dale, I'm-- I'm sure she's okay.

27:22.250 --> 27:23.916
Jesus, look at it!

27:24.708 --> 27:26.458
Oh, those used to be roads.

27:26.541 --> 27:28.000
That amount of water?

27:28.708 --> 27:30.666
The levees must have broken.

27:33.208 --> 27:34.791
How are we gonna get up there?

27:41.000 --> 27:45.750
Okay, so just-- so we're clear,
we get you up the road, you and your boat,

27:45.833 --> 27:49.625
and, uh, we get to tag along from there?
We film whatever we want.

27:49.708 --> 27:53.125
Yeah, yeah, sure.
But can this thing go any faster?

27:55.500 --> 27:56.958
Not really.

27:57.041 --> 28:00.416
They like to keep, uh, Doug and me here
with the hand-me-downs.

28:00.500 --> 28:02.875
Piece-of-crap van's over 20 years old.

28:02.958 --> 28:04.833
I mean, look at that camera.

28:04.916 --> 28:07.625
They shoot porn on better stuff than that.

28:12.541 --> 28:13.791
Billy!

28:14.458 --> 28:15.375
Billy, slow down!

28:15.458 --> 28:18.916
-Slow down? You hurry the fuck up.
-Wait up, damn it!

28:19.000 --> 28:20.250
Okay, come on.

28:21.500 --> 28:22.625
What?

28:27.125 --> 28:28.875
Shit!

28:38.541 --> 28:39.875
Goddamn it!

28:41.125 --> 28:42.500
Fucking ruined, man.

28:43.750 --> 28:46.333
What? What the fuck was that?

28:46.416 --> 28:49.125
-I don't know.
-There's a lot of shit in the water.

28:50.500 --> 28:52.541
Find this fucking key.

28:54.125 --> 28:56.000
Oh my God! Billy!

28:56.083 --> 28:58.291
Get off!

28:59.333 --> 29:01.083
Billy!

29:05.791 --> 29:06.916
Rachel!

29:07.000 --> 29:08.625
No.

29:10.291 --> 29:11.666
Bi-- Billy!

29:11.750 --> 29:13.208
Hey!

29:13.291 --> 29:16.375
Billy! Billy, no!

29:20.583 --> 29:21.416
Rachel!

29:24.708 --> 29:25.875
Hey, Mr. Olson!

29:25.958 --> 29:26.875
Hey!

29:26.958 --> 29:28.791
-Don't leave us!
-Billy!

29:28.875 --> 29:30.041
-Shark!
-A shark!

29:30.125 --> 29:33.333
Shark! Shark!

29:40.875 --> 29:42.375
No, Billy, don't!

29:42.458 --> 29:44.625
-No!
-No! Billy!

29:50.666 --> 29:52.458
Fuck!

29:53.041 --> 29:55.625
You son of a… Fuck!

29:58.708 --> 29:59.958
Fuck. Fuck!

30:07.791 --> 30:10.833
No! No! No!

30:17.375 --> 30:20.250
Does this mean
we have to get new foster parents?

30:21.291 --> 30:23.833
-Oh my God!
-Holy--

30:32.125 --> 30:34.791
Don't look, Will. Don't look.

30:55.250 --> 30:56.375
Help!

30:56.916 --> 30:58.750
Please help!

30:59.333 --> 31:02.875
The branches. Can't get them off me!

31:02.958 --> 31:04.458
Help!

31:04.541 --> 31:06.541
Please help me!

31:06.625 --> 31:07.833
Hello?

31:09.041 --> 31:09.916
Hello?

31:10.000 --> 31:12.583
Look, I'm-- I'm calling for help, okay?

31:12.666 --> 31:15.333
Just… just, just stay there!

31:15.416 --> 31:17.333
I'm stuck!

31:17.416 --> 31:19.666
I'm stuck, and the water's rising!

31:19.750 --> 31:22.125
I'm calling.
Look, I'm calling right now, okay?

31:22.208 --> 31:26.458
-No, there's no time!
-I mean, there's sharks all around you!

31:26.541 --> 31:29.583
They just ripped two people
to fucking pieces!

31:29.666 --> 31:31.708
Trust me, I know.

31:37.625 --> 31:40.791
Okay, listen. Hey, what's your name?

31:40.875 --> 31:43.666
Dakota!

31:43.750 --> 31:45.791
Dakota, I'm pregnant.

31:48.083 --> 31:49.500
And I'm not…

31:50.916 --> 31:56.000
I am not gonna have him die here,
before he gets to take his first breath.

32:01.125 --> 32:04.500
Before I get to see… see his face.

32:16.083 --> 32:17.250
Dakota?

32:18.625 --> 32:20.041
Are you still there?

32:20.875 --> 32:22.083
Oh!

32:38.041 --> 32:40.416
Come on. Come on.

32:41.375 --> 32:42.750
God, help me.

32:50.083 --> 32:50.958
Please!

32:52.125 --> 32:53.833
Okay, I'm coming!

32:55.083 --> 32:56.875
Okay. Oh my God.

33:03.958 --> 33:04.958
Okay.

33:06.666 --> 33:07.625
Okay.

33:16.791 --> 33:18.250
Okay.

33:24.041 --> 33:25.208
Okay…

34:25.250 --> 34:26.625
Okay.

34:43.958 --> 34:44.958
Okay.

34:51.916 --> 34:54.833
You're okay. You're okay.

34:55.500 --> 34:56.916
You got this.

34:57.000 --> 34:58.000
I got this.

34:58.083 --> 35:01.458
Okay. Yeah. Okay.

35:48.791 --> 35:50.666
Come on. You can do it.

35:50.750 --> 35:51.833
Not now.

36:03.791 --> 36:05.916
Okay. Okay.

36:48.916 --> 36:50.958
Okay, you got it!

36:55.666 --> 36:57.166
Okay.

36:59.541 --> 37:00.833
That's it!

37:20.375 --> 37:21.250
Okay.

37:41.000 --> 37:41.916
Okay.

38:11.583 --> 38:12.708
Thank you.

38:21.791 --> 38:24.875
14 inches of rain
falling in the last 12 hours.

38:24.958 --> 38:28.833
Even as Hurricane Henry moves inland,
a PDS flood alert has been issued.

38:28.916 --> 38:30.375
Shit.

38:30.458 --> 38:33.208
The Willow River has jumped its banks,
and the Shasta…

38:33.291 --> 38:34.708
Jesus Christ.

38:34.791 --> 38:36.708
-A flood alert…
-What am I looking at?

38:37.333 --> 38:40.250
That's Dakota's house. And that's…

38:44.041 --> 38:45.208
That's Nellie.

38:47.916 --> 38:48.875
What's a Nellie?

38:49.833 --> 38:53.791
Nellie's the pregnant great white
we've been tracking the last three years.

38:53.875 --> 38:56.166
Great white, as in shark?

38:57.250 --> 38:58.583
Right.

39:02.750 --> 39:05.416
Whatever happens,
you keep that thing rolling, okay?

39:06.250 --> 39:10.458
If Nellie found a way up there,
then maybe the bull sharks--

39:13.750 --> 39:15.416
Jesus Christ.

39:16.666 --> 39:18.708
Oh, shit.

39:40.333 --> 39:43.250
-Shit.
-Do you think they're already inside?

39:46.250 --> 39:47.541
We should close it.

39:48.958 --> 39:50.875
Till we figure out what we're doing.

40:36.916 --> 40:37.916
Come on.

40:53.000 --> 40:54.541
-Dee!
-Whoa!

40:54.625 --> 40:55.833
-Shit! Dee!
-Dee!

40:55.916 --> 40:58.208
Dee! Hold on!

41:04.916 --> 41:07.041
Dee, hold on!

41:17.166 --> 41:18.791
-Ron!
-Shit!

41:18.875 --> 41:19.833
Dee.

41:21.583 --> 41:22.750
I'm coming, Dee!

41:22.833 --> 41:25.583
No. Ron! No!

41:25.666 --> 41:27.916
-Ron!
-I'm coming, hold on!

41:30.250 --> 41:31.083
Ron!

41:35.791 --> 41:37.750
You're all right. It's all right.

41:39.416 --> 41:42.250
It's fine. Hey, hey, hey. Hey, it's okay.

41:54.083 --> 41:55.083
What was that?

42:01.708 --> 42:03.666
The whole town's coming apart.

42:07.208 --> 42:08.291
Thank you.

42:11.500 --> 42:12.833
Are you here alone?

42:17.500 --> 42:19.041
Yeah.

42:19.125 --> 42:22.416
Where are your parents?

42:22.500 --> 42:25.250
Dad died a long time ago, and…

42:26.166 --> 42:28.416
Mom-- my mom a few months back.

42:30.541 --> 42:31.833
I'm sorry.

42:39.125 --> 42:42.083
So what do we…?
What do we do? What's our plan?

42:42.708 --> 42:43.708
You're asking me?

42:43.791 --> 42:44.916
I am from New York.

42:45.000 --> 42:47.583
I don't know shit
about floods or hurricanes.

42:48.958 --> 42:50.208
Uh…

42:51.791 --> 42:53.208
We could stay here.

42:54.375 --> 42:55.875
Here is-- Here is safe.

42:55.958 --> 42:57.083
For now.

42:59.666 --> 43:02.041
Can you, uh…?
Can you access the roof from here?

43:02.125 --> 43:04.083
Yeah, it's an easy climb.

43:04.166 --> 43:09.333
Okay, so i-- if we stay here,
we should let people know we're inside.

43:09.416 --> 43:13.666
You know, helicopters, rescue teams,
those sorts of things?

43:13.750 --> 43:15.416
Okay, uh…

43:15.500 --> 43:18.875
Yeah, like some… some sort of signal.

43:18.958 --> 43:21.166
Yeah, a sig-- A signal.

43:21.250 --> 43:22.458
Okay.

43:22.541 --> 43:25.458
Huh…

43:25.541 --> 43:27.500
Ooh. Ugh.

43:28.666 --> 43:30.250
-Hm…
-You okay?

43:31.041 --> 43:32.000
Yeah.

43:33.000 --> 43:34.208
I'm fine, but, uh…

43:36.166 --> 43:37.708
I think it's starting.

43:39.875 --> 43:42.041
S-- starting, you mean, like, the…

43:42.833 --> 43:44.791
-Like, the actual--
-Yeah.

43:45.958 --> 43:48.250
The actual.

43:57.791 --> 43:58.708
Okay.

44:07.458 --> 44:09.333
We gotta get outta here.

44:09.416 --> 44:10.333
Are you crazy?

44:11.000 --> 44:14.166
There-- there's sharks out there, in here.

44:14.250 --> 44:16.250
Except for on top of this damn table.

44:16.916 --> 44:18.125
Where I'm staying.

44:18.208 --> 44:20.166
I don't wanna go nowhere.

44:23.250 --> 44:25.125
Look around.

44:25.208 --> 44:27.458
The water was just under the windows.

44:27.541 --> 44:29.541
Not anymore, it's creeping up.

44:29.625 --> 44:32.666
It's gonna keep doing that
until we drown or get eaten.

44:33.750 --> 44:35.250
So, how do we even--

44:35.333 --> 44:37.250
I think we need to distract them.

44:37.333 --> 44:40.166
Or… Or find something.

44:40.875 --> 44:43.750
Give us enough time
to get outside and up on that roof.

44:44.500 --> 44:46.208
How the hell are we gonna do that?

44:50.208 --> 44:51.125
Well…

44:52.875 --> 44:56.625
I was thinking,
maybe we can find something.

44:57.958 --> 44:58.791
Okay?

45:00.375 --> 45:02.208
Down in the basement.

45:44.625 --> 45:45.958
Did it work?

45:46.041 --> 45:47.041
Yeah.

45:47.125 --> 45:49.750
Someone flies by, they'll see us.

45:49.833 --> 45:51.166
Hey, look.

45:51.250 --> 45:54.041
The contractions, they're…
They're more frequent.

45:54.125 --> 45:55.958
-Oh, shit.
-"Shit" is right.

45:56.041 --> 46:00.000
Now listen, we need to know how close I am
and how much time we've got.

46:00.708 --> 46:01.541
Why?

46:01.625 --> 46:05.458
Why? 'Cause this whole damn house
is coming apart, that's why.

46:06.375 --> 46:07.958
Or it's gonna flood over.

46:08.041 --> 46:09.041
Exactly.

46:09.125 --> 46:11.416
Yeah. Okay.

46:11.500 --> 46:15.125
All right, so… how do we do it?
How do we find out?

46:15.208 --> 46:18.250
Okay. I'm gonna need you to go down there.

46:18.333 --> 46:20.750
I'm gonna need you
to see how big my opening is.

46:22.250 --> 46:24.166
-Excuse me?
-Trust me.

46:24.250 --> 46:26.458
I don't wanna do this
any more than you do.

46:26.541 --> 46:29.333
-We need to know how far along I am.
-Which means?

46:29.416 --> 46:32.791
You need to see
how close my kid is to squeezing through.

46:32.875 --> 46:35.750
-What?!
-Now, I'm gonna throw the blanket aside.

46:35.833 --> 46:38.250
When I do, take a good look in there.

46:38.333 --> 46:40.458
You're gonna measure it with your eyes,

46:40.541 --> 46:43.000
and you're gonna tell me
how big the opening is.

46:43.833 --> 46:47.541
-How? How do I measure it?
-Just eye measure it, okay? Best you can.

46:48.208 --> 46:50.041
-In inches or…?
-Yes!

46:50.125 --> 46:51.833
-In inches.
-Okay.

46:52.583 --> 46:53.500
Okay.

46:53.583 --> 46:56.416
Three, two, one.

46:59.041 --> 47:01.625
Oh, God!

47:01.708 --> 47:04.750
What? Something wrong? Does it look bad?

47:04.833 --> 47:07.666
-I'm not really sure.
-What do you mean you're not sure?

47:07.750 --> 47:10.291
I mean, I see something.
Something inside there.

47:10.375 --> 47:11.666
-I think. Sorry.
-Okay.

47:11.750 --> 47:13.625
That-- that-- I think that's the head.

47:13.708 --> 47:15.666
-Yeah. Yeah, maybe.
-How big is it?

47:17.125 --> 47:19.166
Okay.

47:19.250 --> 47:22.583
I'd say… I'd say…

47:24.500 --> 47:29.000
Two, three inches, I think.

47:29.083 --> 47:30.208
Was that good?

47:30.291 --> 47:32.708
"Good" in the sense
that the baby's coming soon.

47:34.000 --> 47:34.916
So not good?

47:35.000 --> 47:38.208
Not in the situation we're currently in.

47:38.291 --> 47:39.250
No.

47:42.875 --> 47:45.333
Come on, everyone. Pick up the pace!

47:45.416 --> 47:47.916
We lost signal.
There's no tracking, no maps.

47:48.000 --> 47:49.583
Oh, shit.

47:50.333 --> 47:53.916
Wind's coming in pretty hard right now.
The whole grid is probably down.

47:55.166 --> 47:57.083
Dakota's probably cut off too.

47:58.041 --> 48:01.083
We might be the only help coming.
We gotta go.

48:02.041 --> 48:03.333
Hey, pack light.

48:03.416 --> 48:05.958
The more weight, the slower we move, okay?

48:06.041 --> 48:08.375
Uh… are you sure this is safe?

48:08.458 --> 48:13.125
We're heading up the I-17
in a Zodiac in a Category 5 storm

48:13.208 --> 48:14.500
with sharks on the loose!

48:14.583 --> 48:17.791
No, I'm pretty fucking sure
that doesn't count as safe.

48:17.875 --> 48:20.083
We don't have time
for any of this bullshit.

48:20.166 --> 48:22.833
Are you coming, or are you swimming back?

48:22.916 --> 48:25.875
If the tech's down,
how do we even know where to go?

48:29.958 --> 48:33.041
All right! Let's move!

48:44.958 --> 48:47.041
Look, there's one.

48:50.708 --> 48:52.083
There's one over there too.

48:53.625 --> 48:55.208
What are we gonna do, Ron?

48:57.833 --> 48:58.750
Okay.

48:59.833 --> 49:02.208
We just wait 'em out
before swimming down there.

49:04.500 --> 49:08.000
Saw some big-ass steaks in the fridge.
Should be good as bait.

49:08.875 --> 49:11.041
Perfect. I'll start there.

49:12.625 --> 49:13.791
Then what?

49:15.750 --> 49:16.750
Yeah.

49:17.875 --> 49:19.666
Guns, I guess.

49:21.708 --> 49:24.958
Don't grab too much stuff.
You gotta be able to swim back up.

49:26.708 --> 49:28.791
It's just like the swamps.

49:28.875 --> 49:30.000
I'll be all right.

49:33.833 --> 49:35.208
Ron?

49:36.000 --> 49:38.666
Mr. Olson doesn't like us
going down to the basement.

49:41.750 --> 49:42.750
Well…

49:44.291 --> 49:46.833
Mr. Olson ain't with us anymore now,
is he?

49:46.916 --> 49:48.333
Uh-uh.

49:49.583 --> 49:51.208
Right.

49:51.291 --> 49:52.250
Well, then…

49:54.125 --> 49:55.666
Fuck Mr. Olson!

49:58.041 --> 49:59.166
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

49:59.250 --> 50:00.083
Fuck him.

50:01.833 --> 50:02.833
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

50:02.916 --> 50:04.500
Fuck Mr. Olson!

50:04.583 --> 50:06.708
-Yeah, fuck Mr. Olson!
-Fuck that dickhead.

50:06.791 --> 50:08.166
Fuck that motherfucker!

50:08.250 --> 50:10.958
-Fuck him!
-Fuck that fucking-- Fuck Mr. Olson!

50:11.041 --> 50:11.958
What the hell?

50:16.208 --> 50:17.208
Mr. Olson!

50:17.291 --> 50:18.875
We were just talking about you.

50:18.958 --> 50:20.125
That goddamn thing

50:20.208 --> 50:23.375
bit my motherfucking arm
and butt cheek clean off!

50:29.916 --> 50:32.916
We're heading
up the I-17 right now, on boat.

50:34.583 --> 50:35.833
I'm sorry, did you say boat?

50:35.916 --> 50:37.875
Don't ask. Long story.

50:37.958 --> 50:40.708
But this should keep us clear
of the worst of it, right?

50:40.791 --> 50:44.041
Yeah. You're in one of the calmer pockets,
so you're good for now.

50:44.125 --> 50:46.000
Great. Let's keep it that way.

50:46.666 --> 50:48.208
Hey, Dale?

50:48.291 --> 50:49.666
The levee is broken.

50:49.750 --> 50:54.250
The water is just gonna keep rising,
so if you're getting someone out, hurry.

51:00.291 --> 51:01.833
It's rising, fast.

51:05.291 --> 51:08.500
We don't have a choice.
We have to get outta here.

51:10.083 --> 51:11.833
You said you saw a boat out there?

51:11.916 --> 51:15.458
Yeah, it's from those guys earlier.
The ones that…

51:18.291 --> 51:20.375
But, I mean, it's far.

51:21.041 --> 51:23.000
We can still stay here for a bit.

51:23.083 --> 51:25.250
Everything's gonna flood eventually.

51:25.333 --> 51:27.416
Okay. Okay, so…

51:28.041 --> 51:28.958
So what do we do?

51:38.375 --> 51:39.708
Ooh.

51:42.708 --> 51:44.500
Damn.

51:47.333 --> 51:48.333
No.

51:57.541 --> 51:58.583
God.

51:59.208 --> 52:00.333
Hey.

52:01.791 --> 52:05.458
It's not safe out here right now, okay?
It's not safe.

52:07.291 --> 52:12.625
So you just gotta stay in there
just a little longer, okay?

52:16.041 --> 52:19.458
Please. Please.

52:52.958 --> 52:54.125
Fuck it.

53:01.875 --> 53:03.458
What are you doing?

53:06.833 --> 53:08.666
I'm gonna go get that boat.

53:09.750 --> 53:11.625
But there's sharks out there.

53:12.375 --> 53:17.000
My uncle once said something
about how vibrations,

53:17.083 --> 53:20.166
they mimic the distress signals
of… of injured fish.

53:20.250 --> 53:21.625
Your uncle?

53:21.708 --> 53:23.416
Yeah, he's a marine biologist.

53:23.500 --> 53:26.875
He works with sharks.
Tags 'em, tracks 'em, that sort of thing.

53:29.375 --> 53:33.041
I need to round up anything
that works on batteries and vibrates.

53:33.125 --> 53:35.750
Hey, do you have any painkillers?

53:36.666 --> 53:40.583
You know, in case this thing
is really… happening now.

53:41.291 --> 53:42.125
Uh, lemme check.

53:50.000 --> 53:51.541
All right.

53:51.625 --> 53:52.500
Here.

53:53.500 --> 53:54.791
Thanks.

53:58.625 --> 54:00.416
Motherfucker.

54:20.541 --> 54:21.833
Smart.

54:21.916 --> 54:23.166
Yeah, well.

54:24.666 --> 54:27.666
Let's hope Uncle Dale knows
what the fuck he's talking about.

54:30.541 --> 54:32.208
Okay, now, Nellie.

54:33.166 --> 54:35.208
We know she's bigger than this boat.

54:35.291 --> 54:39.916
-And what about those bull sharks?
-Wanna know about bull sharks?

54:40.000 --> 54:42.833
What the hell is…

54:42.916 --> 54:43.958
Look!

54:45.500 --> 54:47.000
Holy shit.

55:13.750 --> 55:14.750
Dakota?

55:20.416 --> 55:21.916
Thank you.

55:42.875 --> 55:45.375
What about your mom, Rachel?
She… she make it?

55:58.333 --> 55:59.708
You left us.

56:01.041 --> 56:03.708
-What are you talking about?
-Out there.

56:03.791 --> 56:06.166
You were gonna get
in that truck and drive off.

56:07.083 --> 56:09.458
Yeah, to get some help.

56:09.541 --> 56:10.625
Yeah, right.

56:10.708 --> 56:12.833
Hey, don't you sass me, Ray.

56:13.416 --> 56:14.291
It's Ron!

56:15.791 --> 56:17.333
That's what I said, man.

56:17.416 --> 56:18.791
I went to get help, Ron.

56:18.875 --> 56:20.791
Now you got to do the same for me.

56:20.875 --> 56:24.916
Get out there, man, get me some help.
I got, like, a-- a goddamn nub here.

56:25.000 --> 56:26.375
Out there?

56:26.458 --> 56:27.625
Yeah, in the water.

56:28.708 --> 56:31.666
Where there's at least
three bull sharks swimming around?

56:31.750 --> 56:33.500
Where your wife just got killed?

56:34.500 --> 56:36.708
Yeah, you know what sharks are like, okay?

56:36.791 --> 56:39.166
They don't eat kids, man.
They don't like 'em.

56:39.250 --> 56:43.458
Right? They don't like the way they taste
or smell or something. It's… It's science.

56:43.541 --> 56:46.375
Just like how, uh,
dogs don't eat their own turds.

56:46.458 --> 56:49.583
One time, Johnny Watkins' dog
took a shit and ate it all.

56:49.666 --> 56:51.375
Fuck Johnny Watkins, okay?

56:51.458 --> 56:53.916
Fuck his dog, and fuck you, okay?

56:54.000 --> 56:56.833
Get in there, get me some help.
I'm fucking dying here.

56:57.916 --> 56:58.916
Whoa.

57:00.583 --> 57:04.041
-This is a lot of money.
-Put that down, man. That's not yours.

57:04.125 --> 57:06.333
"United States Treasury."

57:06.416 --> 57:10.333
"Monthly foster stipend, $1,500."

57:13.791 --> 57:16.291
You get all that money to take care of us?

57:16.375 --> 57:18.416
You living on steaks while we eat bread?

57:18.500 --> 57:21.083
Hey, it's not like that, son, okay?

57:21.166 --> 57:22.791
I-- I promise.

57:22.875 --> 57:24.833
I-- I-- I love you kids.

57:30.000 --> 57:31.250
You know what? Listen.

57:31.333 --> 57:34.208
I still got one good arm left.
Don't think I won't use it.

57:34.291 --> 57:36.958
I'm not fucking asking you now!
I'm telling you!

57:37.041 --> 57:39.125
Get back in that fucking water, go get--

57:39.208 --> 57:42.458
In case you haven't noticed, Billy,
it's all flooded.

57:42.541 --> 57:44.166
There's no people.

57:44.250 --> 57:45.625
No roads, no cars.

57:45.708 --> 57:48.958
Not to mention,
there's goddamn sharks out there.

57:51.541 --> 57:54.250
So you can do it your fucking self.

57:55.416 --> 57:58.250
You money-grabbing, one-armed,
half-an-ass piece of shit!

57:58.333 --> 57:59.625
Little son of a bitch!

58:02.375 --> 58:03.375
You little asshole!

58:20.958 --> 58:22.791
You kicked me in my face, you bitch!

59:32.625 --> 59:34.333
Hey, go! Go, go.

59:34.416 --> 59:35.750
While they're busy, go!

59:36.750 --> 59:38.250
Go! Hurry!

01:00:52.875 --> 01:00:54.500
Come on, Ron!

01:00:55.916 --> 01:00:57.958
-Come on!
-Come on. Ron!

01:01:08.541 --> 01:01:09.791
Shit!

01:01:11.166 --> 01:01:14.416
Ooh, it's okay. It's all right.

01:01:14.500 --> 01:01:15.375
You're okay.

01:01:17.916 --> 01:01:20.583
It's all right. Whoa, it's okay.

01:01:20.666 --> 01:01:21.833
We're okay.

01:01:55.083 --> 01:01:56.750
Come on. Come on.

01:02:23.375 --> 01:02:24.333
Shit!

01:02:46.875 --> 01:02:48.500
Where the hell are they going?

01:03:44.958 --> 01:03:47.416
After 17 inches of rain,

01:03:47.500 --> 01:03:50.250
several towns are cut off
from any rescue attempts.

01:03:50.916 --> 01:03:56.125
And multiple rivers jumping their banks,
causing even more deadly flooding.

01:03:56.208 --> 01:04:01.166
There has been no communication
from Sandy Beach, Annieville, or Whitford.

01:04:01.250 --> 01:04:03.958
We're sending out prayers
to the people of those towns.

01:04:04.666 --> 01:04:07.250
I can't imagine
the dangers they're facing.

01:04:11.250 --> 01:04:13.000
Jesus Christ.

01:04:14.125 --> 01:04:17.458
Everything's flooded.
I've never seen anything like this.

01:04:17.541 --> 01:04:20.041
Just go straight through.

01:04:20.125 --> 01:04:22.833
We should be able
to reach Annieville from the west.

01:04:25.083 --> 01:04:27.666
Why did you decide to study sharks?

01:04:28.375 --> 01:04:31.958
Isn't the idea usually
to stay away from them, not get closer?

01:04:32.041 --> 01:04:35.333
I grew up by the banks
of the Zambezi River.

01:04:35.416 --> 01:04:36.958
It's a beautiful place.

01:04:37.041 --> 01:04:40.625
But there's one animal
we fear the most in the river.

01:04:40.708 --> 01:04:41.583
Sharks.

01:04:41.666 --> 01:04:44.375
No, the hippopotamus.

01:04:44.458 --> 01:04:48.958
They are fast, powerful,
and extremely territorial.

01:04:50.333 --> 01:04:53.916
One day,
I was looking for crayfish in the river,

01:04:54.000 --> 01:04:56.958
when a hippo appeared and came for me.

01:04:57.041 --> 01:05:00.125
I heard my mother scream
on the riverbank, and I froze.

01:05:01.333 --> 01:05:05.875
And just when he was about to take me,
he suddenly stopped and twitched,

01:05:05.958 --> 01:05:08.000
like he was being choked or something.

01:05:08.750 --> 01:05:12.250
Two powerful bull sharks
were attacking it.

01:05:12.333 --> 01:05:16.250
And in that moment, I saw something
in the eyes of the hippopotamus

01:05:16.333 --> 01:05:18.250
I had never seen before.

01:05:18.333 --> 01:05:19.541
Fear.

01:05:19.625 --> 01:05:22.250
So did you run back to your hut
and get a spear?

01:05:22.333 --> 01:05:26.333
No. I ran back to my apartment,
called the police, and had me some pizza.

01:05:26.416 --> 01:05:30.083
We lived in Mozambique,
not the fucking Jungle Book.

01:05:30.166 --> 01:05:31.375
Oh.

01:05:32.083 --> 01:05:33.125
Sorry.

01:05:33.208 --> 01:05:35.500
And so, from that moment on,

01:05:35.583 --> 01:05:37.958
I became really interested
in this creature

01:05:38.041 --> 01:05:41.291
that can put fear
in the eyes of a river hippo.

01:05:48.333 --> 01:05:52.083
Did you ever find anything
that these bull sharks are afraid of?

01:05:52.791 --> 01:05:54.916
They just don't like bigger sharks.

01:05:55.000 --> 01:05:58.041
And certain electrical currents
can disorient them.

01:05:58.625 --> 01:06:00.708
So otherwise, they don't do fear.

01:06:01.916 --> 01:06:03.458
Signal's back up!

01:06:08.666 --> 01:06:09.708
Oh, Jesus.

01:06:10.416 --> 01:06:11.333
What is that?

01:06:12.166 --> 01:06:14.750
The dots? Sharks.

01:06:14.833 --> 01:06:16.541
That's Annieville.

01:06:18.916 --> 01:06:20.250
Wait, slow down.

01:06:54.833 --> 01:06:57.500
